@startumltitle Order standing transferautonumberskinparam sequenceMessageAlign centerskinparam responseMessageBelowArrow falseskinparam maxMessageSize 260actor "Customer" as customerparticipant "Customer Web App\n(React SPA)" as spa  participant "Core Banking API \n(FastAPI)" as apidatabase "PostgreSQL" as dbcustomer -> spa : On Scheduled Transfers fill in:\n source account, recipient IBAN, amount, currency, description, frequencyspa -> spa : Validates the form; the chosen frequency is mapped to a cron  expression e.g. monthly = '0 0 1 * *'spa -> api : POST /standing-transfers {sourceAccountid, recipientAccountNumber, amount, currency, description, cronExpression}api -> api : Authenticates the user (token) and Validates the payload (amount > 0, cron syntax, source != recipient)api -> db : SELECT ... FROM accounts WHERE id = :source OR account_number = :recipientdb --> api : account rowsalt source not owned by user / account not ACTIVE / recipient not found / invalid cronapi --> spa : 403 / 404 / 422 errorspa --> customer : Shows error message else data is Validatesapi -> api : Computes next_run_at = first occurrence of the cron expression after now()api -> db : INSERT INTO Scheduled_transactions (source_account_id, target_account_id, currency, amount, description, cron_expression, next_run_at,\n status = 'ACTIVE')db --> api : new row idapi --> spa : 201 Created {id.nextRunAt, status = ACTIVE}spa --> customer : Shows the new entry on the Scheduled Transfers listend Note over api,db : The Scheduled job Worker later finds ACTIVE rows with\nnext_run_at <= now() and executes them through the Core Banking API\n(seperate flow)@enduml